  6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

  You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these four ways:

  a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by the
Corresponding Source fixed on a durable physical medium (such as a
CD-ROM).

  b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a written
offer, valid for at least three years, to give anyone who possesses
the object code a copy of the Corresponding Source for all the
software in the product, at a price no more than the cost of
physically performing the distribution.

  c) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (such as a web site), at no charge, and providing equivalent
access to the Corresponding Source in the same way through the same
interface.

  d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (such as a web site), at no charge, and allowing anyone to
copy the Corresponding Source in the same way through the same
interface.

